WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.790
- [Narrator] Opioids are
drugs that are prescribed

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.970
to treat moderately severe or severe pain.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.660
Examples of these drugs
include hydrocodone,

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.550
oxycodone, morphine,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.333
hydromorphone, and methadone.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.083
Heroin, an illegal
drug, is also an opioid.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.720
In order to understand how opioids work,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.900
it's important to know
how your body feels pain.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.010
The process begins

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.690
when something harmful
happens to your body.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.970
Information about this harm is
converted to a nerve signal.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.760
The signal passes along nerves

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.683
to your spinal cord and brain.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.503
In your brain, the signal
is perceived as pain.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.800
Opioid drugs affect how you feel pain.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.143
They attach to structures
called opioid receptors.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.180
These receptors are found
on cells in your brain,

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.600
spinal cord, and other areas of your body.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.513
Opioids act on these receptors
to make you feel less pain.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.470
These drugs also have different
effects in other areas.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.540
For example, opioids act

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.240
on the reward pathway in your brain.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.400
This causes a release of
a chemical called dopamine

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.043
that results in a happy feeling or high.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.870
Opioids may also cause slower breathing,

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.570
and they may cause reduced
motion of your intestines,

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.463
resulting in constipation.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.410
For most people, when opioids
are taken as prescribed

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:40.250
for a short time, they are
fairly safe and effective.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.910
But these drugs can be taken in ways

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.040
that weren't prescribed,
such as taking too many,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.940
taking them to get high, or
giving them to someone else.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.410
Misusing these drugs can raise your risk

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.450
of developing drug tolerance,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.913
dependence, addiction and overdose.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.090
Tolerance means the drug is
less effective over time.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.580
This can happen when opioid
receptors become less sensitive

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.570
to the effects of the drug.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.750
As a result, more of the
drug needs to be taken

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.493
for you to get pain relief.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.790
Dependence happens if
a person has symptoms

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.920
when they stop using the drug.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.670
When the drug is removed or
withdrawn, you feel sick.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.660
This sickness is called withdrawal.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.040
Opioid withdrawal has flu-like symptoms

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.450
that include restlessness and anxiety,

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.080
muscle aches, inability to sleep,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.590
watery eyes and runny
nose, nausea and vomiting,

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:46.423
stomach cramps and diarrhea,
and dilated or widened pupils.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.400
Opioid addiction is a brain disease

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.490
where you have an overwhelming
craving for the drug.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.330
You can't stop taking the drug,

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.363
despite the harm it may cause you.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.510
Addiction is not the same as dependence.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.990
You can be tolerant of a
drug or dependent on a drug

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.063
without being addicted to it.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.310
Finally, opioid overdose is a condition

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.190
where taking too much of the drug

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.790
can cause life-threatening
symptoms or even death.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:22.160
The symptoms of opioid
overdose can include confusion,

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.610
feeling very sleepy or not
alert, nausea and vomiting,

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.560
constricted or small
pupils, unconsciousness,

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.293
slow or stopped breathing, and death.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.060
According to the Centers
for Disease Control,

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.723
over 100 Americans die each
day from opioid overdoses.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.980
If you have questions about opioids

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.270
or if you or someone
close to you needs help

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.340
for an opioid use disorder,

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.163
talk to your healthcare provider.

